      "side": 1,
      "message": "LAM does, as you saw in the vmx_get_untagged_addr(), which will be used by the host to emulate for npVM. XSAVE is not for now as the code of having guest_can_use(X86_FEATURE_XSAVES) are moved to the pkvm hypervisor, e.g., kvm_load_guest_xsave_state/kvm_load_host_xsave_state. To keep the similar implementation with vmx_vcpu_after_set_cpuid(), also set the governed feature for XSAVES, in case this might be needed in the future for the npVM. VMX is another feature set by vmx_vcpu_after_set_cpuid(), but this feature is not needed for us so didn\u0027t add.",
